module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.stable_citation_mutable_referent

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data stable_citation_mutable_referent: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "stable_citation_mutable_referent" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**stable citation, mutable referent** (an identifier that names a thing correctly and forever, while the CONTENT served for it is replaced underneath. ",

    "Distinct from `positional_citation`, and the difference is what makes it worse: a `file:line` pointer goes stale under an edit above it, and re-reading the file EXPOSES that — the symbol is not there, or a different one is. ",

    "Here re-reading the citation CONFIRMS the wrong answer, because the identifier still resolves, still returns content of the expected shape, and reports no error. ",

    "There is no red anywhere. ",

    "Receipt (2026-09-02, gunbc#10042): a GitHub Actions JOB ID was cited as the source of a floor measurement. ",

    "A job id names the job; the logs API serves the LATEST ATTEMPT. ",

    "A rerun replaces the attempt, so job 100217416636 served six budget-refused identities when first read and thirteen when read back, and the second reading was byte-identical to a DIFFERENT job id — two ids, one attempt. ",

    "A cross-run comparison built on those readings appeared to compare two runs while one side had been replaced underneath, and the damage ran in BOTH directions: a near-disjointness claim that was simply false, and a real bucket migration that was retracted as unfounded because it could no longer be reproduced through the citation that found it. ",

    "The second is the more expensive error — a true finding withdrawn, downstream prose rewritten in four places to remove it, and a merge rule changed — and it is the one a reader would not think to look for, because a retraction feels like the conservative move. ",

    "THE DEFAULT CITATION IS THE TRAP AND THE PINNED ONE IS THE REMEDY, and both were measured rather than assumed: `gh run view --job <id> --log` serves the latest attempt, but the attempt-pinned REST path — `/repos/OWNER/REPO/actions/runs/RUNID/attempts/N/logs` still serves attempt 1 in full. ",

    "Recovering it confirmed the original six-row reading exactly, and confirmed that `an_empty_receipt_series_leaves_the_live_tree_unmeasured_rather_than_held` is INTERRUPTED in attempt 1 and COMPLETED-OVER-COST in attempt 2 — a real migration across the two populations, not the artifact it was briefly retracted as. ",

    "So the class is not that the earlier subject is destroyed; it is that the ORDINARY way of citing it silently resolves to a different one, and a reader who re-reads the same citation to check gets agreement instead of a contradiction. ",

    "**Recognition rule: before comparing two readings of one producer, ask whether the producer serves a STABLE SUBJECT for a fixed citation — not whether the citation is well-formed. ",

    "An identifier that addresses a CONTAINER (a job, a branch, a latest, a mutable tag, a rolling window) serves whatever currently occupies it, so two readings of one citation are two subjects and their DELTA is uninterpretable. ",

    "Cite the thing that cannot be replaced — the attempt, the commit, the immutable artifact — or capture the content at read time and say when.** The receipt worth keeping is that this survived the diligence that should have caught it: the same author had, that morning, REFUSED to file a transcribed measurement on the §6 grounds that no producer owned the number, and then built a delta out of a producer that mutates what it serves for a fixed id. ",

    "Naming the instrument is not sufficient if the instrument does not serve a stable subject. ",

    "One diagnostic tell for the delta itself, preserved here from gunbc#10130 where it was measured against this same receipt: the two readings were differenced into a `3 -> 6 -> 13` upward trend with a memory-pressure mechanism attached, the `3` having additionally come from a different head — and monotone growth is precisely what independent draws at a fixed distance from a budget do NOT produce. ",

    "The shape that made the artifact persuasive was the evidence against it, so the tell is available BEFORE the referent is re-checked: a delta through a container-addressing citation that arrives already fitting a story is the reading to distrust first.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
